// Enemy stat blocks. Add a type here and it can be spawned by name.
//
// Mobs collide with the world like the player does, so `radius`/`height` are
// their physical box and `jumpForce` caps how high they can climb. At GRAVITY
// -28 the apex is jumpForce^2 / 56 blocks — every type here clears a
// one-block step and nothing taller, so they have to path around cliffs
// rather than levitate. That apex figure assumes home's own gravity
// specifically; entities/mobs.js scales the actual launch speed by the
// local body's real gravity strength at the moment of the jump, so the same
// PHYSICAL apex height holds everywhere, not just at home — see its own
// comment on why an unscaled jump was the actual cause of mobs drifting off
// into space on a low-gravity moon.
//
// Every type gets a distance-based throw (`throwRange`/`throwDmg`/
// `throwCooldown`/`throwSpeed`/`projectile`) AND a close-range
// `meleeStyle` finisher that always hits harder than the throw
// (`meleeDmg` > `throwDmg` on every type below) — `meleeStyle` picks which
// generic melee routine entities/mobs.js's 'melee' state plays out:
//   'lunge' — a fast, committed dash into melee range, Ghoul's old dropkick.
//   'slam'  — a windup then a heavy, ground-shaking downward slam, Wretch's
//             old powerbomb.
//   'swipe' — a quick, no-windup strike with no repositioning — the new,
//             snappier third style, for the faster/lighter attackers.
//
// Two roam the home planet; every OTHER body gets its own single, unique
// monster keyed to its own alien theme (world/alienBiomes.js) — see
// entities/mobs.js's THEME_MOB table for the theme -> type mapping used by
// the night-time spawner.

