// Hand tools and heavy machinery: what they cost to build, how much faster
// they mine their specialty than bare hands, and how hard they hit.
//
// BondBlocks leans modern-industrial rather than medieval — the four hand
// tools are the entry tier, then each of the three machine lines (digging,
// forestry, drilling) escalates through increasingly serious equipment. A
// bigger machine mines faster AND clears a radius around the block you're
// aiming at, not just that one block — see `radius` below.
//
// Every entry:
//   categories  — which world/blocks.js mining categories it's good at.
//                 Aiming it at anything else mines at bare-hand speed.
//   speedMul    — bare-hand mining time (world/blocks.js BASE_MINE_SECONDS)
//                 is divided by this.
//   radius      — 0 for hand tools. For machines, breaking the aimed block
//                 also breaks every same-category block within this many
//                 blocks of it — a small blast of clearance rather than one
//                 block at a time, which is what makes a machine feel like
//                 a machine.
//   meleeDamage — these all double as melee weapons; an excavator should
//                 flatten something a hand drill barely dents.
//
// Tool ids start at 300, clear of block ids (0-99), weapon ids (100+) and
// vehicle ids (200+).

